place:castel-nuovo a schema:Place ;
    schema:additionalType "Landmark" ;
    schema:description "Castel Nuovo, often called Maschio Angioino, is a medieval castle located in front of Piazza Municipio and the city hall in central Naples, Campania, Italy. Its scenic location and imposing size makes the castle, first erected in 1279, one of the main architectural landmarks of the city. It was a royal seat for kings of Naples, Aragon and Spain until 1815."@en ;
    schema:disambiguatingDescription "The medieval castle on the seafront; Lewis is riding toward it along the bomb-damaged Via Partenope when he is nearly caught by one of the German delayed-action mine explosions."@en ;
